## The look, figures: the Python Bpy.xtl writes for a walking figure
## (LookPieces.xtl) -- an armature of nine bones from arrays, parts
## skinned to its bones (the head rigidly, the tunic and the legs shared
## between two bones), the clips walk and idle keyed on the bones, the
## export and the file read back -- pinned.

"lk:" u_se< "LookPieces"

"the figure:"
lk:figure c_at lk:f_ile "look-figure"
